# Template for /opt/zfvg/.env on the server (deploy/README.md, "Directory layout").
#
# Copy this file to /opt/zfvg/.env, replace the two placeholder values, then
#   chmod 600 /opt/zfvg/.env
# The real file must never be committed. ".env" is listed in the repository's
# .gitignore, and tools/check_secrets.py fails if a file named .env is tracked.
#
# The cTrader CLI reads these when it is started with --environment-variables. The
# variable name is the option name with "-" written as "_" (image README,
# "Configuration by environment variable":
# https://github.com/spotware/ctrader-console-docker).
#
# The password is NOT here. The CLI reads it only from a file (--pwd-file, or
# PWD_FILE in the environment); batch commands such as "run" reject --password
# (https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-cli/faq/). Put it in
# /opt/zfvg/secrets/ctrader-cli.pwd (README, step 7).

# cTrader ID (user name or e-mail address) that owns the trading account.
CTID=your-ctrader-id

# Trading account login number of the FTMO Free Trial or Challenge account.
ACCOUNT=your-account-number
